IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg10-14a-kinds`

-- LAYER 1, regulation 27: when a relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE.  Regulation 27 gives several routes into the duty, each introduced by "if", "when" or "in relation to": a business relationship is
-- established (1)(a); an occasional transaction over £800 that is a transfer of funds (1)(b); suspicion (1)(c); doubt (1)(d); an occasional
-- transaction of £12,000 or more (2); a cash transaction of £10,000 or more by a high value dealer (3); a casino transaction of £2,000 or more
-- (5); a letting (7A); an art transaction or storage (7C); a cryptoasset exchange machine (7D); a cryptoasset transfer of £800 (7E); and the
-- existing-customer occasions (8).  Each route has its own function.  A route whose "if" fails answers JUST FALSE (Marginal readings, (a)).
-- `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` gathers the routes by hand (ruling E1, option B), and is the
-- answer other parts take as seam S-1.  What the measures are is regulation 28 (module mlr1-reg28-cdd-measures).
-- Money is a NUMBER of pounds sterling.  A transaction is the core's `Transaction`; it is an occasional transaction when it is not carried out as part of a business relationship (reg 3(1)).

§ `Regulation 27(1) -- The general occasions`

-- reg 27(1)(a).  A relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures if the person establishes a business relationship.
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): the keel's regulation 4 answers whether there is a business relationship.
-- src:765 | (1) A relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures if the person—
-- src:766 | (a) establishes a business relationship;
-- src:767 | (b) carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation exceeding £800;
-- src:768 | (c) suspects money laundering or terrorist financing; or
-- src:769 | (d) doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification.
@ref reg 27(1)(a) (src:765-769)
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person establishes that business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(1)(a) the relevant person establishes a business relationship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person establishes that business relationship`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must apply customer due diligence measures if the person— (a) establishes a business relationship" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person— (a) establishes a business relationship" (Marginal readings, (a): what was established is not a business relationship)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 4 has not answered whether there is a business relationship

-- reg 27(1)(b).  ... if the person carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9
-- of the funds transfer regulation exceeding £800.
@ref reg 27(1)(b) (src:767-767)
GIVEN transaction IS A Transaction
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(1)(b) the relevant person carries out an occasional transaction that is a transfer of funds exceeding 800 pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF transaction's `carried out as part of a business relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person— (b) carries out an occasional transaction" (Marginal readings, (a): the transaction is part of a business relationship, so not an occasional transaction, reg 3(1))
        IF transaction's `a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` AND transaction's `value in sterling, linked operations taken together` GREATER THAN `the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to a transfer of funds ... exceeding £800" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(1)(c).  ... if the person suspects money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 27(1)(c) (src:767-768)
GIVEN `the relevant person suspects money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(1)(c) the relevant person suspects money laundering or terrorist financing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person suspects money laundering or terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person— (c) suspects money laundering or terrorist financing" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(1)(d).  ... if the person doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of
-- identification or verification.
@ref reg 27(1)(d) (src:769-769)
GIVEN `the relevant person doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(1)(d) the relevant person doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person— (d) doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained" (Marginal readings, (a))

§ `Regulation 27(2) to (4) -- Occasional transactions`

-- reg 27(2).  A relevant person who is not a letting agent, a high value dealer, an art market participant, a cryptoasset exchange provider of the
-- kind referred to in paragraph (7D) or (7E), a custodian wallet provider of the kind referred to in paragraph (7E) or a casino must also apply
-- customer due diligence measures if the person carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to £12,000 or more, whether the transaction is
-- executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
-- Paragraph (7E) names "a cryptoasset exchange provider and a custodian wallet provider" without limit, so the exclusion removes both whole kinds
-- (fork F-27(2) in NOTES): a person who is any of those kinds is outside this route.
-- src:770 | (2) A relevant person who is not a letting agent, a high value dealer, an art market participant, a cryptoasset exchange provider of the kind referred to in paragraph (7D) or (7E), a custodian wallet provider of the kind referred to in paragraph (7E) or a casino must also apply customer due diligence measures if the person carries out an occasional transaction that amounts to £12,000 or more, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
@ref reg 27(2) (src:770-770)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 27(2) the amount of 12000 pounds sterling` MEANS 12000

@ref reg 27(2) (src:770-770)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      transaction IS A Transaction
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2) the relevant person carries out an occasional transaction of 12000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN k YIELD k EQUALS `letting agent` OR k EQUALS `high value dealer` OR k EQUALS `art market participant` OR k EQUALS `cryptoasset exchange provider` OR k EQUALS `custodian wallet provider` OR k EQUALS `casino`) `the kinds of the relevant person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person who is not a letting agent, a high value dealer, an art market participant, a cryptoasset exchange provider of the kind referred to in paragraph (7D) or (7E), a custodian wallet provider of the kind referred to in paragraph (7E) or a casino" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF transaction's `carried out as part of a business relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person carries out an occasional transaction" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF transaction's `value in sterling, linked operations taken together` AT LEAST `reg 27(2) the amount of 12000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an occasional transaction that amounts to £12,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(4).  A transaction does not cease to be a "transaction in cash" for the purposes of paragraph (3) if cash is paid by or on behalf of a
-- party to the transaction (a) to a person other than the other party to the transaction for the benefit of the other party, or (b) into a bank
-- account for the benefit of the other party to the transaction.
-- src:772 | (4) A transaction does not cease to be a “transaction in cash” for the purposes of paragraph (3) if cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction—
-- src:773 | (a) to a person other than the other party to the transaction for the benefit of the other party, or
-- src:774 | (b) into a bank account for the benefit of the other party to the transaction.
@ref reg 27(4) (src:772-774)
GIVEN `the transaction is paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction into a bank account for the benefit of the other party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(4) the transaction is a transaction in cash for the purposes of paragraph (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction is paid in cash` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party` OR `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction into a bank account for the benefit of the other party` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3(1) says "cash" means notes, coins or travellers' cheques, and none is paid in this transaction, so it is not "in cash"; paragraph (4) only keeps a transaction in cash in the two cases it names (changed 2026-11-05 on review: it answered NOTHING). Whether travellers' cheques are cash is not decided by this function: the input `the transaction is paid in cash` is a fact the caller states

-- reg 27(3).  A high value dealer must also apply customer due diligence measures if that dealer carries out an occasional transaction in cash that
-- amounts to £10,000 or more, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
-- src:771 | (3) A high value dealer must also apply customer due diligence measures if that dealer carries out an occasional transaction in cash that amounts to £10,000 or more, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
@ref reg 27(3) (src:771-771)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 27(3) the cash amount of 10000 pounds sterling` MEANS 10000

@ref reg 27(3) (src:771-771)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      transaction IS A Transaction
      `reg 27(4) the transaction is a transaction in cash for the purposes of paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(3) the high value dealer carries out an occasional transaction in cash of 10000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `high value dealer` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A high value dealer must also apply customer due diligence measures if that dealer carries out" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not a high value dealer)
        IF transaction's `carried out as part of a business relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that dealer carries out an occasional transaction" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF `reg 27(4) the transaction is a transaction in cash for the purposes of paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND transaction's `value in sterling, linked operations taken together` AT LEAST `reg 27(3) the cash amount of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 27(4) the transaction is a transaction in cash for the purposes of paragraph (3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction is in cash has not been answered (Marginal readings, (h): the paragraph (4) answer was not given by the caller)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an occasional transaction in cash that amounts to £10,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))

§ `Regulation 27(5) to (7) -- Casinos`

-- reg 27(6).  A transaction is within this paragraph if it consists of (a) the wagering of a stake, including (i) the purchase from, or exchange with,
-- the casino of tokens for use in gambling at the casino; (ii) payment for use of gaming machines; and (iii) the deposit of funds required to take
-- part in remote gambling; or (b) the collection of winnings, including the withdrawal of funds deposited to take part in remote gambling or
-- winnings arising from the staking of such funds.
DECLARE `reg 27(6) kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 27(6)(a) the wagering of a stake`
    `reg 27(6)(a)(i) the purchase from, or exchange with, the casino of tokens for use in gambling at the casino`
    `reg 27(6)(a)(ii) payment for use of gaming machines`
    `reg 27(6)(a)(iii) the deposit of funds required to take part in remote gambling`
    `reg 27(6)(b) the collection of winnings`
    `reg 27(6)(b) the withdrawal of funds deposited to take part in remote gambling or winnings arising from the staking of such funds`
    `reg 27(6) another transaction`

-- src:776 | (6) A transaction is within this paragraph if it consists of—
-- src:777 | (a) the wagering of a stake, including—
-- src:778 | (i) the purchase from, or exchange with, the casino of tokens for use in gambling at the casino;
-- src:779 | (ii) payment for use of gaming machines (within the meaning of section 235 of the Gambling Act 2005 ); and
-- src:780 | (iii) the deposit of funds required to take part in remote gambling; or
-- src:781 | (b) the collection of winnings, including the withdrawal of funds deposited to take part in remote gambling (within the meaning of section 4 of the Gambling Act 2005) or winnings arising from the staking of such funds.
@ref reg 27(6) (src:776-781)
GIVEN kind IS A `reg 27(6) kind of transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(a) the wagering of a stake` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(a)(i) the purchase from, or exchange with, the casino of tokens for use in gambling at the casino` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(a)(ii) payment for use of gaming machines` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(a)(iii) the deposit of funds required to take part in remote gambling` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(b) the collection of winnings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6)(b) the withdrawal of funds deposited to take part in remote gambling or winnings arising from the staking of such funds` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(6) another transaction` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A transaction is within this paragraph if it consists of— (a) the wagering of a stake, including ...; or (b) the collection of winnings, including ..." (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 27(7).  In determining whether a transaction amounts to £2,000 or more for the purposes of paragraph (5), no account is to be taken of winnings
-- from a previous transaction which had not been collected from the casino, gaming machine or remote gambling, but are being re-used in the
-- transaction in question.
-- src:782 | (7) In determining whether a transaction amounts to £2,000 or more for the purposes of paragraph (5), no account is to be taken of winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected from the casino, gaming machine or remote gambling, but are being re-used in the transaction in question.
@ref reg 27(7) (src:782-782)
GIVEN `the amount of the transaction, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
      `the winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected but are being re-used in the transaction, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 27(7) the amount of the transaction for the purposes of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    `the amount of the transaction, in pounds sterling` MINUS `the winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected but are being re-used in the transaction, in pounds sterling`

-- reg 27(5).  A casino must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any transaction within paragraph (6) that amounts to £2,000 or more,
-- whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
-- src:775 | (5) A casino must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any transaction within paragraph (6) that amounts to £2,000 or more, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked.
@ref reg 27(5) (src:775-775)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 27(5) the amount of 2000 pounds sterling` MEANS 2000

@ref reg 27(5) (src:775-775)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 27(7) the amount of the transaction for the purposes of paragraph (5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(5) the casino carries out a transaction within paragraph (6) of 2000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `casino` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A casino must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any transaction" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not a casino)
        IF `reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to any transaction within paragraph (6)" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF `reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `reg 27(7) the amount of the transaction for the purposes of paragraph (5)` AT LEAST `reg 27(5) the amount of 2000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that amounts to £2,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction is within paragraph (6) has not been answered

§ `Regulation 27(7A) to (7E) -- Letting agents, art market participants and cryptoasset businesses`

-- reg 27(7A).  A letting agent must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any occasional transaction which consists of the
-- conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land (within the meaning given in regulation 13(7)) (i) for a term of a month or more, and (ii) at a
-- rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
-- src:783 | (7A) A letting agent must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any occasional transaction which consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land (within the meaning given in regulation 13(7))—
-- src:784 | (i) for a term of a month or more, and
-- src:785 | (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
@ref reg 27(7A) (src:783-785)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      transaction IS A Transaction
      `the transaction consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of the letting, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7A) the letting agent concludes an agreement for the letting of land for a month or more at a monthly rent of 10000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `letting agent` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A letting agent must also apply customer due diligence measures" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not a letting agent)
        IF transaction's `carried out as part of a business relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to any occasional transaction" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF `the transaction consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land` AND `the term of the letting, in months` AT LEAST 1 AND `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 13(4)(b)(ii) the monthly rent of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) for a term of a month or more, and (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(7B).  The letting agent must apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (7A) in relation to both the person by whom the land is
-- being let, and the person who is renting the land.
DECLARE `reg 27(7B) party to the letting` IS ONE OF
    `reg 27(7B) the person by whom the land is being let`
    `reg 27(7B) the person who is renting the land`
    `reg 27(7B) another person`

-- src:786 | (7B) The letting agent must apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (7A) in relation to both the person by whom the land is being let, and the person who is renting the land.
@ref reg 27(7B) (src:786-786)
GIVEN party IS A `reg 27(7B) party to the letting`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7B) the letting agent must apply customer due diligence measures in relation to the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `reg 27(7B) the person by whom the land is being let` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(7B) the person who is renting the land` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 27(7B) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (7B) names the person letting and the person renting

-- reg 27(7C).  An art market participant must also apply customer due diligence measures (a) in relation to any trade in a work of art (within the
-- meaning given in regulation 14), when the firm or sole practitioner carries out, or acts in respect of, any such occasional transaction, whether
-- executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked, whose value amounts to £10,000 or more; (b) in relation to the
-- storage of a work of art (within the meaning given in regulation 14), when it is the operator of a freeport and the value of the works of art so
-- stored for a person, or series of linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more.
-- src:787 | (7C) An art market participant must also apply customer due diligence measures—
-- src:788 | (a) in relation to any trade in a work of art (within the meaning given in regulation 14), when the firm or sole practitioner carries out, or acts in respect of, any such occasional transaction, whether executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked, whose value amounts to £10,000 or more;
-- src:789 | (b) in relation to the storage of a work of art (within the meaning given in regulation 14), when it is the operator of a freeport and the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more.
@ref reg 27(7C) (src:787-789)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      transaction IS A Transaction
      `the transaction is a trade in a work of art, carried out or acted in respect of by the firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7C)(a) the art market participant carries out or acts in respect of an occasional transaction in a work of art of 10000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `art market participant` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An art market participant must also apply customer due diligence measures" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not an art market participant)
        IF transaction's `carried out as part of a business relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any such occasional transaction" (Marginal readings, (a))
        IF `the transaction is a trade in a work of art, carried out or acted in respect of by the firm or sole practitioner` AND transaction's `value in sterling, linked operations taken together` AT LEAST `reg 14(1)(d) the art transaction or storage value of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any trade in a work of art ... whose value amounts to £10,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))

@ref reg 27(7C)(b) (src:787-789)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `the art market participant is the operator of a freeport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7C)(b) the art market participant is the operator of a freeport storing works of art of 10000 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `art market participant` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An art market participant must also apply customer due diligence measures" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not an art market participant)
        IF `the art market participant is the operator of a freeport` AND `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 14(1)(d) the art transaction or storage value of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to the storage of a work of art ..., when it is the operator of a freeport and the value ... amounts to £10,000 or more" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(7D).  A cryptoasset exchange provider of the kind who operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money,
-- or money for cryptoassets, must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any such transaction carried out using that machine.
-- src:790 | (7D) A cryptoasset exchange provider of the kind who operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets, must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to any such transaction carried out using that machine (and for the purposes of this paragraph “money” and “cryptoasset” have the same meanings as they have in regulation 14A(1)).
@ref reg 27(7D) (src:790-790)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `the person operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is carried out using that machine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7D) the cryptoasset exchange provider carries out a transaction using its machine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `cryptoasset exchange provider` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A cryptoasset exchange provider of the kind who operates a machine ... must also apply customer due diligence measures" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is not a cryptoasset exchange provider)
        IF `the person operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets` AND `the transaction is carried out using that machine` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to any such transaction carried out using that machine" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(7E).  Without prejudice to paragraph (7D), a cryptoasset exchange provider and a custodian wallet provider must also apply customer due
-- diligence measures in relation to a cryptoasset transfer which is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value (taken together
-- with any other cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked).
-- src:791 | (7E) Without prejudice to paragraph (7D), a cryptoasset exchange provider and a custodian wallet provider must also apply customer due diligence measures in relation to a cryptoasset transfer which is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value (taken together with any other cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked).
@ref reg 27(7E) (src:791-791)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      transfer IS A `Cryptoasset transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(7E) the cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider carries out a cryptoasset transfer of 800 pounds or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `cryptoasset exchange provider` `the kinds of the relevant person` OR elem `custodian wallet provider` `the kinds of the relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a cryptoasset exchange provider and a custodian wallet provider must also apply customer due diligence measures" (Marginal readings, (a): the person is neither)
        IF transfer's `value in sterling, linked transfers taken together` AT LEAST `the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a cryptoasset transfer which is equal to or exceeds the equivalent in cryptoassets of £800 in value" (Marginal readings, (a))

§ `Regulation 27(8) and (9) -- Existing customers`

-- reg 27(8).  A relevant person must also apply customer due diligence measures (za) when the relevant person has any legal duty in the course of the
-- calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing any information which is relevant to the risk assessment for that
-- customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer; (zb) when the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to
-- fulfil any duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015; (a) at other appropriate times to existing customers on a risk based
-- approach; (b) when the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment have changed.
-- src:792 | (8) A relevant person must also apply customer due diligence measures—
-- src:793 | (za) when the relevant person has any legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing any information which—
-- src:794 | (i) is relevant to the relevant person’s risk assessment for that customer, and
-- src:795 | (ii) relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer, including information which enables the relevant person to understand the ownership or control structure of a legal person, trust, foundation or similar arrangement who is the beneficial owner of the customer;
-- src:796 | (zb) when the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil any duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015 ;
-- src:797 | (a) at other appropriate times to existing customers on a risk based approach;
-- src:798 | (b) when the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed.
@ref reg 27(8) (src:792-798)
GIVEN `the relevant person has a legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing information that is relevant to the risk assessment for that customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(8)(za) the relevant person has a legal duty to contact an existing customer to review beneficial ownership information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person has a legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing information that is relevant to the risk assessment for that customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(za) when the relevant person has any legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer" (Marginal readings, (a))

@ref reg 27(8)(zb) (src:796-796)
GIVEN `the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(8)(zb) the relevant person has to contact an existing customer to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(zb) when the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil any duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(8)(a).  The text gives no fixed period for re-applying customer due diligence to existing customers: it says "at other appropriate times ... on a risk based approach".
-- So there is no date or interval to compute; whether this time is appropriate is a judgement the text leaves to the person applying it, and arrives as a BOOLEAN input (a stated gap).
@ref reg 27(8)(a) (src:797-797)
GIVEN `it is appropriate, on a risk based approach, to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers at this time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(8)(a) it is an appropriate time to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is appropriate, on a risk based approach, to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers at this time` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) at other appropriate times to existing customers on a risk based approach" (Marginal readings, (a))

@ref reg 27(8)(b) (src:798-798)
GIVEN `the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(8)(b) the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer have changed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) when the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed" (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 27(9).  For the purposes of paragraph (8), in determining when it is appropriate to take customer due diligence measures in relation to existing
-- customers, a relevant person must take into account, among other things, (a) any indication that the identity of the customer, or of the customer's
-- beneficial owner, has changed; (b) any transactions not reasonably consistent with its knowledge of the customer; (c) any change in the purpose or
-- intended nature of its relationship with the customer; (d) any other matter which might affect its assessment of the risk in relation to the customer.
-- src:799 | (9) For the purposes of paragraph (8), in determining when it is appropriate to take customer due diligence measures in relation to existing customers, a relevant person must take into account, among other things—
-- src:800 | (a) any indication that the identity of the customer, or of the customer's beneficial owner, has changed;
-- src:801 | (b) any transactions which are not reasonably consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer;
-- src:802 | (c) any change in the purpose or intended nature of the relevant person's relationship with the customer;
-- src:803 | (d) any other matter which might affect the relevant person's assessment of the money laundering or terrorist financing risk in relation to the customer.
@ref reg 27(9) (src:799-803)
GIVEN `it has taken into account any indication that the identity of the customer, or of the customer's beneficial owner, has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account any transactions which are not reasonably consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account any change in the purpose or intended nature of the relevant person's relationship with the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account any other matter which might affect the relevant person's assessment of the money laundering or terrorist financing risk in relation to the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(9) the relevant person has taken into account what paragraph (9) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken into account any indication that the identity of the customer, or of the customer's beneficial owner, has changed` AND `it has taken into account any transactions which are not reasonably consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer` AND `it has taken into account any change in the purpose or intended nature of the relevant person's relationship with the customer` AND `it has taken into account any other matter which might affect the relevant person's assessment of the money laundering or terrorist financing risk in relation to the customer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person must take into account, among other things—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 27(10).  In this regulation, "cryptoasset" and "cryptoasset transfer" have the meanings given by regulation 64B: pointers outside this part.
-- (Another part answers regulation 64B; no seam id is registered for it, so these take its answers as inputs, to fill at the merge.)
-- src:804 | (10) In this regulation, “cryptoasset” and “cryptoasset transfer” have the meanings given by regulation 64B (cryptoasset transfers: interpretation).
@ref reg 27(10) (src:804-804)
GIVEN `reg 64B the thing is a cryptoasset` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(10) the thing is a cryptoasset` MEANS
