        IF `reg 64B the thing is a cryptoasset` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 64B the thing is a cryptoasset` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset” and “cryptoasset transfer” have the meanings given by regulation 64B" (regulation 64B answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by regulation 64B

@ref reg 27(10) (src:804-804)
GIVEN `reg 64B the transfer is a cryptoasset transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(10) the transfer is a cryptoasset transfer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 64B the transfer is a cryptoasset transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 64B the transfer is a cryptoasset transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset” and “cryptoasset transfer” have the meanings given by regulation 64B" (regulation 64B answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by regulation 64B

§ `Regulation 27 -- The relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures (seam S-1)`

-- Hand-gathered from the sixteen routes above (ruling E1, option B: guidance for gathering by hand); each route has its own answer (option C).
